{:edb/db-before-t 1735 :edb/db-after-t 1736 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535048 50 #inst "2026-10-08T15:35:32.122Z" 13194139535048 true] [17592186124518 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328528 13194139535048 true] [17592186124573 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328521 13194139535048 true] [17592186124750 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535048 true] [17592186124750 1100 "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=8x,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty .\n$$" 13194139535048 true] [17592186124750 1100 "Identify the following surface:\n\n$z^{2} = 8x, - ∞ < y < ∞$." 13194139535048 false] [17592186124750 1145 "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis and $p=2.$" 13194139535048 true] [17592186124751 1017 #edb/ref 17592186121525 13194139535048 false] [17592186124751 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328535 13194139535048 true] [17592186124751 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535048 true] [17592186124751 1100 "Identify the surface $2x^{2} - 4z^{2} - 4x - y - 16z - 12 = 0$." 13194139535048 false] [17592186124751 1100 "Identify the surface $2{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}-4x-y-16z-12=0.$" 13194139535048 true] [17592186124751 1145 "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}-4x-y-16z-12 & =0 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}-2x)-4({z}^{2}+4z)-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2[(x-1)^{2}-1]-4[(z+2)^{2}-4]-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-2-4(z+2)^{2}+16-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2}-y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2}-y+2 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2} & =y-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-2).$" 13194139535048 true] [17592186124863 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535048 true] [17592186124863 1100 "Identify the surface $4x^{2} + 8y^{2} + 2z^{2} - 8x + 8z + 4 = 0$." 13194139535048 false] [17592186124863 1100 "Identify the surface $4{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-8x+8z+4=0.$" 13194139535048 true] [17592186124863 1145 "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-8x+8z+4 & =0 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-2x)+8{y}^{2}+2({z}^{2}+4z)+4 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x-1)^{2}-1]+8{y}^{2}+2[(z+2)^{2}-4]+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-4+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2}-8+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2}-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-1)^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2}-8 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{4(x-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{8{y}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{2(z+2)^{2}}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an ellipsoid centered at $(1,0,-2).$" 13194139535048 true] [17592186328521 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328522 13194139535048 true] [17592186328521 1089 "q-164543" 13194139535048 true] [17592186328521 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535048 true] [17592186328521 1100 "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n4{y}^{2}-3{z}^{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$" 13194139535048 true] [17592186328521 1113 #uuid "04bdbcd8-5184-50ec-95c0-30cd62912fcf" 13194139535048 true] [17592186328521 1145 "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $b=\\frac{1}{2},\\,c=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.$" 13194139535048 true] [17592186328522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328523 13194139535048 true] [17592186328522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328524 13194139535048 true] [17592186328522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328525 13194139535048 true] [175921